  "notes": "Warren J. Smith, Modern Lens Design, 2nd ed., Figure 16.17 (page number not visible in the photos). Book: EFL 95.79, BFL 11, NA -0.0627 (F/8.0), GIH 3.35 (HFOV=2.00), PTZ/F 10.33, VL 7.58, infinite conjugate. Glass: BSF10 entered as BASF10 (Schott, 1.650/39.1 as in the book). The book does not mark the stop; it is placed at surface 1, the front element. The table gives thicknesses without sign; spaces after an odd number of reflections are entered negative, which reproduces the book's VL. The primary mirror is surface 5 (rear of the SF2 block) and the secondary is surface 9; the return path crosses a central zone whose surfaces differ from the outer zone (surfaces 6 and 12 at -234.628). Central obscuration and baffles are not modelled. Discrepancy with the book: entered as printed, the table gives a focal length of -120.8 and a back focus of -28.3 instead of the book's 95.79 and 11; no single plane-row placement, mirror placement or sign change reproduces the book, so a value in the printed table may be misread or misprinted.",
